<title>VENEZUELA: PdVSA to remit $8 bln to Venezuela treasury in 96.</title>
<headline>PdVSA to remit $8 bln to Venezuela treasury in 96.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan state owned oil company PdVSA will remit some 3.4 trillion bolivars ($8 billion), or 14 percent of Venezuelan gross domestic product, in petro-revenues to the national treasury this year, company president Luis Giusti said.</p>
<p>&quot;Using the newly calculated average price of $17 per barrel, PdVSA will provide around 14 percent of Venezuelan gross domestic product to the treasury, that's to say 3.4 trillion bolivars,&quot; Giusti told reporters.</p>
<p>At the official average exchange rate for the year of 422 bolivars per dollar, that translates into $8 billion. In 1995 PdVSA remitted 980 billion bolivars ($5.6 billion), according to company figures.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
